          "title": "You'll want to know: commemorō, commemorāre",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "commemorō, commemorāre — \"to recall, to mention\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Senex victōriās veterēs commemorābat. The old man was recalling old victories."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "commemorō, commemorāre, commemorāvī, commemorātum: to bring something fully to mind, and so to mention it. English commemorate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "commemorō is built on memorō, \"to bring to mind, to tell of\", with con- (EtymDB); memorō comes from memor, \"mindful\". English commemorate comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
