          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "memorō, memorāre — \"to tell of, to relate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Poētae multa dē bellīs memorant. Poets tell many things about wars."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "memorō, memorāre, memorāvī, memorātum. Poetic and historical in tone; Vergil opens his poem by asking the Muse to tell him the causes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "memorō is built on memor, \"mindful\" (EtymDB), which is inherited from a Proto-Indo-European root meaning \"to remember\". English memory comes from memoria, of the same family."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
