          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "referō, referre — \"to report; to carry back\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nūntius omnia quae vīderat ducī rettulit. The messenger reported to the leader all that he had seen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "referō, referre, rettulī, relātum, irregular like ferō. Ad senātum referre: to put a matter before the senate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "referō is built on ferō, \"to carry\", with re-, \"back\" (EtymDB): to carry back, and so to bring back word. English refer comes from it, and relate from its participle."
            }
          ]
        },
